  "scientific_findings": [
    "The constrained candidate improves future MSE over unconstrained integral initialization by 44.54 to 49.07 percent, but remains 7.86 to 8.10 times the original encoder MSE.",
    "All six protections fail against the encoder for every seed and both steps, while all pass against the unconstrained integral reference.",
    "The candidate misses 16 trajectory-rule triggers and adds 2 extra triggers per seed/step; the encoder misses 17 and adds 0. Fewer misses cannot offset the extra-trigger protection failure.",
    "Lower closed-loop history MSE than the encoder and controlled initial hidden-state norm coexist with much worse future prediction. This specific fixed-model energy-ball replacement does not meet the future objective.",
    "The comparison does not establish a unique physical cause of the transfer failure, real hidden-state recovery, new label classification performance or a general impossibility of joint training."
  ],
